{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 48, :comments ["<b>And YHWH spoke to Moses on this very day.</b> In three places 'on this very day' is said. It is said of Noah: ״בְּעֶצֶם הַיּוֹם הַזֶּה בָּא נֹחַ וגוֹ״ (Genesis 7) — at the brightness of the day, because the men of his generation were saying: At such-and-such a time, if we sense him, we will not let him enter the ark, and not only that — we will take clubs and axes and split the ark. Said the Holy One, blessed be He: I will bring him in at midday, and whoever has the power to object, let him come and object. In Egypt it is said: ״בְּעֶצֶם הַיּוֹם הַזֶּה הוֹצִיא יהוה״ (Exodus 12), because the Egyptians were saying: At such-and-such a time, if we sense them, we will not let them leave, and not only that — we will take swords and weapons and kill them. Said the Holy One, blessed be He: I will take them out at midday, and whoever has the power to object, let him come and object. So too here, at the death of Moses, 'on this very day' is said, because Israel were saying: At such-and-such a time, if we sense it — we will not let him; a man who took us out of Egypt and split the sea for us and brought the manna down for us and gave us the quail and brought the well up for us and gave us the Torah — we will not let him. Said the Holy One, blessed be He: I will bring him in at midday, etc. (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:35.836692874Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}